// THE EXEMPTION AS FILED, VERBATIM. The operator pasted the filed form on 2026-09-11: reason "I do
// not persist eBay data", with the Additional information text below exactly as submitted.
//
// WHAT THIS RECEIPT DOES NOT ESTABLISH, and an earlier revision of it did claim: that eBay
// ADJUDICATED the disclosure. eBay activates a keyset once the developer subscribes or opts out, so
// activation follows the exemption SELECTION; it does not decide whether the accompanying
// free-text disclosure of listing-attribute retention is within the reason selected. The activation
// is recorded as its own observation (receipt_ebay_browse_production_access_observed). Whether the
// retained profile is covered stays open at step_ebay_exemption_applicability.
data receipt_ebay_exemption_filing_recorded: ActionReceipt = ActionReceipt {
  receipt_id: "ebay-exemption-filing-recorded",
  evidence: ObservedFact {
    subject: "Marketplace Account Deletion exemption for the Gunbai LLC Production keyset, reason: I do not persist eBay data",
    observation: "filed, not adjudicated. Additional information, verbatim: Read-only use of the Buy Browse API with an application (client-credentials) token, for internal procurement of our own server hardware. We do not store any eBay user personal data (no usernames, user IDs, EIAS tokens, or buyer/seller contact details), and our data model has no field that can hold them. We retain listing attributes only (item ID, title, price, shipping cost, condition, item specifics, and seller feedback percentage/score without any seller identity) for internal purchase review. -- the keyset activated after submission, which follows the opt-out selection and does not decide the disclosure",
    observed_at: "2026-09-11",
  },
}

