// THIS STEP READS OPEN AND THE EVIDENCE SAYS IT IS SATISFIED, REPORTED RATHER THAN DISCHARGED.
// The staging run recorded below refused at NO GCP ACCESS TOKEN, which the bracket reaches only
// AFTER the bucket check, so the origin is DurableOriginAllocated and this step's work is done.
// It is left StepOpen deliberately: discharging needs an ActionReceipt carrying ReceiptEvidence,
// and authoring one from a refusal I ran myself would mint a receipt shape nobody reviewed for
// this subject. Whoever owns receipts here should close it; the evidence is named, not withheld.
data step_storage_bucket_identity: OwnerStep = OwnerStep {
  step_id: "storage-bucket-identity",
  plan_item: "storage-provider-accounts",
  work: DelegatedActionWork {
    instruction: "Declare the durable origin bucket identity and its enrolled scope: which bucket is the origin, what is admitted to it, and under whose credential.",
  },
  start_requirements: [AfterStep { step_id: "storage-r2-declarations-merged" }],
  produces_receipt: "storage-bucket-identity-declared",
  progress: StepOpen,
}

// THE MINT IS NOT OPERATOR WORK AND THIS STEP SAID IT WAS. Operator ruling, relayed 2026-09-12:
// "for any NEW tokens we need, they would need to be acquired/realized via the workflows, not my
// hand minting." The bootstrap token was the hand-minted one and that intervention is already
// discharged; the object-READ token was then minted BY the workflow under it (gunbc#10947, from a
// session). So this step's previous instruction -- execute the mint against the live account --
// described a human doing what an entry does, and it is the reason "the operator must mint the R2
// write token" was carried as a blocker for most of a day. It was withdrawn on that ruling.
//
// WHAT IS ACTUALLY LEFT IS ONE CEREMONY, AND IT IS ITS OWN STEP BELOW. The entry needs a
// short-lived GCP access token at run time to read the bootstrap token out of Secret Manager. That
// is the whole human part, and splitting it out is what stops the delegated work reading as
// operator work again.
data step_storage_access_token_ceremony: OwnerStep = OwnerStep {
  step_id: "storage-access-token-ceremony",
  plan_item: "storage-provider-accounts",
  work: OperatorActionWork {
    intervention: open_operator_intervention(
      identity: "storage-access-token-ceremony",
      subject: "short-lived GCP access token for the mint run",
      instruction: "Supply a short-lived GCP access token to the session that will run the mint entry, as a FILE whose path is exported as GUNBC_GCP_ACCESS_TOKEN_FILE. The entry reads the pinned bootstrap token from Secret Manager with it. Do not paste the value into chat, argv, a worktree file or a receipt - a previous ceremony put a ya29 token into a session transcript and it had to be treated as burned.",
    ),
  },
  start_requirements: [AfterStep { step_id: "storage-bucket-identity" }],
  produces_receipt: "storage-access-token-supplied",
  progress: StepOpen,
}

// MEASURED, NOT ASSUMED: staged in an arm64 session container on 2026-09-12 at public main
// f9d37e43a17, this entry refused at exactly "NO GCP ACCESS TOKEN: no GUNBC_GCP_ACCESS_TOKEN_FILE
// in the environment ... NOTHING CREATED" and at nothing earlier. Its bracket refuses on six typed
// causes, so ONE refusal clears five of them by execution rather than by reading: the bootstrap
// token IS in custody, the account id is present, the bucket IS allocated, and the mint IS
// admitted. The environment was confirmed to carry zero GCP variables first, so the refusal was
// guaranteed and the AccountTokens.Create call was unreachable - a safe probe, not a near miss.
data step_storage_token_mint: OwnerStep = OwnerStep {
  step_id: "storage-token-mint",
  plan_item: "storage-provider-accounts",
  work: DelegatedActionWork {
    instruction: "Run gunbc.cloudflare.r2_token_mint_run run_object_write in a session container - never a remote build, which cannot execute gunbc at all - with the ceremony token in place. Then confirm the pin lands in gunbc.cloudflare.r2_origin, that the value is stored through gunbc.secret_provision, and let instruments/fabric_m0_origin_object_probe establish it by roundtrip.",
  },
  start_requirements: [AfterStep { step_id: "storage-access-token-ceremony" }],
  produces_receipt: "storage-origin-token-minted",
  progress: StepOpen,
}

